      "content": "Even with a small dose, slight changes in how any medication affects your body can be unpredictable, especially with asthma. Beta-blockers can impact the airways for some people, and I cannot estimate what a \"tiny\" dose might do for your specific person. For your safety, please do not try to self-prescribe or adjust dosages of prescription drugs. The safest path is to contact your primary care physician or an urgent care clinic for immediate, personalized guidance.",
